.UPDATE...
Issued at 851 AM PST Sun Nov 1 2026

Satellite imagery this morning shows the cold front south of
Monterey and San Benito counties this morning, working its way
through SLO and towards southern CA. There are a few lingering
showers, mainly over over our waters, though a few reflectivites
can be seen skirting the Big Sur coast and over interior Monterey
County. Expecting drier conditions for the afternoon, with high
temperatures making into the low to mid 60s for most interior
valleys, the upper 50s to low 60s along the coast, and perhaps
only into the upper 40s to mid 50s in the higher elevations of the
region.

