.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1016 AM PST Sun Nov 1 2026

Satellite imagery shows VFR conditions, the cold front out of our
region, and cumulus clouds left in its wake mainly south of the
North Bay and most prevalent over the terrain. A few isolated
showers remain over the waters, though a few may skirt along the
Big Sur coastline through the early afternoon. Expect onshore
winds for much of the region, with winds becoming light and
southerly to variable overnight. Generally think VFR conditions
should prevail, with some high clouds trying to sneak in early
Monday morning. Should we keep enough breaks in the clouds, or
they don`t manifest, we could see some pockets of fog in the North
Bay valleys. Moderate to high confidence in the forecast.


Vicinity of SFO...Generally VFR conditions should prevail around
SFO, with some cumulus clouds bubbling up along the nearby terrain.
Winds should switch onshore by the afternoon, with perhaps a few
gusts to 20-23kt this afternoon. Winds decrease after sunset,
cumulus clouds should dissipate, with weak onshore flow overnight.
Winds should shift to the south early Monday morning. Moderate to
high confidence in the forecast.


SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Mainly VFR conditions should prevail today,
as northwest winds lead to lingering cu over the region. Showers
should hold for a few hours over the coastal waters, and may skirt
the Big Sur Coastline. Otherwise dry conditions prevail and onshore
winds return this afternoon. We may see some gusts to 15-20kt around
KMRY and KSNS through the early evening. Winds then weaken, with
south to southeast flow expected by Monday morning. Moderate to high
confidence in the forecast.

