.MARINE...
(Today through Friday)
Issued at 851 AM PST Sun Nov 1 2026

Rain showers generally south of Pigeon Point will continue this
morning and then taper out by the early afternoon. Moderate to
fresh winds have generally shifted to the north and northwest
behind the front, though some fresh to strong gusts will linger
through the afternoon and evening hours. Hazardous conditions for
small craft are expected and will ease from north to south.
Gentle to moderate breezes and moderate seas will prevail,
building to become rough in the outer waters Tuesday into
Wednesday.

